{
  "slug": "distributed-architect",
  "name": "Distributed Architect",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "A reasoning framework that helps Claude analyze distributed system code changes for correctness before writing code. It provides an always-on boundary detector that recognizes when changes cross component boundaries (state mutations, data serialization, failure handling, new interactions), then loads targeted reasoning checklists on demand. Three slash commands cover the full development lifecycle: /dist-check for coding-time two-pass analysis, /dist-design for architecture trade-off eval...",
  "longDescription": "Ships **3 skills**.\n\n- **Skills** (3): `dist-check` (Two-pass boundary + concurrency analysis on distributed system code changes), `dist-debug` (Backward root-cause tracing from symptoms to cause boundary in distributed systems), `dist-design` (Architecture trade-off analysis for distributed system design decisions)\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install distributed-architect@claude-community` from `Langerrr/distributed-architect`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "antigravity",
    "codex"
  ],
